{
  "id": "m1_culture_v1",
  "name": "Module 1: culture chip (demo scale)",
  "description": "DEMO SCALE: 30 x 20 mm, 0.3 mm deep, one fluidic layer, resin print + hot emboss. Scaled uniformly in x and y by 0.389 (tools/fit_chip.py) from 75 x 25 mm; depths are not scaled (chamber depth 0.5 -> 0.3 mm, channels 0.1 mm) and volume_ul is recomputed by the tool from the new geometry. Channel widths (0.078 mm after scaling) and junctions were clamped up to the 0.2 mm floor, which changed the flow resistances: the clamped channels are about 2.6x wider than scaled, so resistance per length is far lower than the original design and any flow numbers must be re-derived. PORTS 16 -> 5 (limit 6, pitch >= 5 mm): m1_medium_in_1/2/3 merged into m1_factor_1/2/3 (one lane reagent inlet each, an off-chip selector valve picks medium, factor or label); m1_out_1/2/3 merged into m1_out_1 through a collector junction; m1_ctrl_1..6 removed. Lost: simultaneous medium + factor streams (now sequential or pre-mixed), per-chamber harvest and supernatant sampling (all lanes drain to one outlet), and lane isolation. Also removed because they need a second (membrane) layer or a crossing: the 3 branch valves, the 3 pair valves, the signals-only microgrooves m1_sig_1/2/3 (10 um, unprintable; m1_sig_1 also crossed m1_ch_feed_2) and the gas window. Cells load at m1_ipsc_in_1 (shared inlet, also detach reagent and harvest buffer), split three ways, each lane gets its own reagent at a T-junction, flows through an in-line bubble trap into its culture chamber and drains to the shared outlet. Each chamber and channel carries a 'block' naming its CAD block (contracts/blocks.json). Originally: one culture unit per chip, printed twice (control and interaction); GENERATED by cad/generators/m1_culture.py (the generator still emits the 75 x 25 mm design and would overwrite this file).",
  "placeholder": true,
